-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 286  Quest reward spells (21) + the achievement criterion that blocks 60050
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---- 1. Crescent Grove's unearnable achievement ----------------------------
--     Table `achievement_criteria_data` does not have expected data for
--     criteria (Entry: 13512 Type: 0) for achievement 60050.
--
-- 🔴 THIS ONE IS FATAL, NOT COSMETIC, and it is a leftover from the round that
-- fixed its six siblings. `AchievementMgr` treats a MISSING data row as FAILED,
-- not as "no extra condition":
--     AchievementCriteriaDataSet const* data = sAchievementMgr->GetCriteriaDataSet(...);
--     if (!data || !data->Meets(GetPlayer(), unit))
--         continue;
-- so the criterion can never progress and the achievement is unearnable.
--
-- Criterion 13512 read from the DEPLOYED Achievement_Criteria.dbc (not the
-- staging CSV -- the ids are assigned at CSV-append time): Achievement_Id
-- **60050 "Crescent Grove"**, Type **0 = KILL_CREATURE**, Asset_Id **4020007
-- "Master Raxxieth"** (1 spawn, map 823), Quantity 1. Type 0 is in the
-- require-data list at AchievementMgr.cpp:2903.
--
-- 13511 and 13513-13517 all have their rows; **13512 is the only one of the
-- seven that was missed**. Type 0 = ACHIEVEMENT_CRITERIA_DATA_TYPE_NONE, which
-- returns true from both IsValid() and Meets() -- it satisfies the non-null
-- check without adding a condition, exactly as the other 477 type-0 rows do.
-- The creature is already named by the criterion's own Asset_Id, so type 1
-- T_CREATURE would be redundant.
DELETE FROM acore_world.`achievement_criteria_data` WHERE `criteria_id` = 13512;
INSERT INTO acore_world.`achievement_criteria_data` (`criteria_id`,`type`,`value1`,`value2`,`ScriptName`) VALUES
(13512,0,0,0,'');

-- ---- 2. 21 quest reward spells ---------------------------------------------
--     Quest 25621 has `RewardSpell` = 76479 but spell 76479 does not exist,
--     quest will not have a spell reward.
--
-- `ObjectMgr::LoadQuests` drops a RewardSpell / RewardDisplaySpell whose spell
-- is absent, so 28 quests have been handing out nothing on turn-in. 26 distinct
-- spell ids; **21 resolve in the Cata 4.3.4 Spell.dbc** and are added here.
--
-- REACHABILITY WAS CHECKED FIRST, per the ~2,100-orphan-quest lesson -- 17 of
-- the 28 quests have a questgiver and 11 have none at all. Both sets are
-- downported: it is one generator run either way, it clears their log lines
-- too, and 268_ showed the relation layer keeps growing, so a quest that is
-- unreachable today may not be tomorrow. The 11 reachable quests this actually
-- restores a reward for are 13935, 13947, 13974, 13981, 14249, 14270, 25621,
-- 25945, 28044, 28261, 28364.
--
-- 🔴 The overlay trap caught me again while sizing this: querying
-- `WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM spell_dbc ...)` reported **654** missing
-- reward spells. `spell_dbc` holds only CUSTOM rows -- stock spells live in the
-- real Spell.dbc -- so 649 of those were false positives. The true list came
-- from the boot log and `read_server_dbc`.
--
-- Safety scan before shipping, the same one 273_ needed: of the 21, exactly one
-- touches the invisibility family and it is 76629 "Detect: Quest Invis Default"
-- -- aura **19 MOD_INVISIBILITY_DETECT**, which reveals phased content to the
-- player. No MOD_INVISIBILITY (18) and no PHASE (261), so nothing here can hide
-- a player or shift them out of phase.
--
-- CLIENT SIDE ALREADY COMPILED AND DEPLOYED: Spell.dbc 53,277 -> 53,298, 0 ids
-- lost, all 53,277 pre-existing rows byte-identical, written to patch-4 +
-- enGB/patch-enGB-3 + the three WarcraftXLHost checkouts + staging (md5
-- identical across all five). Generator: tools/gen_hyjal_spell_downport_r39.py

DELETE FROM acore_world.`spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (65465,65498,65688,76629,69950,68185,76479,77851,89755,90147,90133,62858,64118,64578,65716,67597,74916,77534,78054,78306,89362);

